This project includes protocol definitions informed by:
- Wireless-Device-Battery-Monitor / BatteryHub (GPL-3.0-or-later, https://github.com/krisgfx9/Wireless-Device-Battery-Monitor).
- Voltide (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Joko).
- HeadsetControl (GPL-3.0, https://github.com/Sapd/HeadsetControl) — wireless headset battery protocols and USB product IDs (Logitech Centurion / G930, Lenovo Wireless VoIP, EPOS H3PRO Hybrid, FIFINE HT6, MCHOSE X9 / V9 Pro, Sony PULSE 3D, Razer BlackShark V2 Pro PlayStation, and SteelSeries / Audeze / Corsair / Logitech headset protocol details).
- libratbag (MIT License, https://github.com/libratbag/libratbag) — Logitech HID++ 1.0 battery registers (`0x07` / `0x0D`) and HID++ 2.0 `0x1001` wireless charging flag.
- OpenRGB (GPL-2.0-or-later, https://gitlab.com/CalcProgrammer1/OpenRGB) — wireless peripheral USB product IDs (Razer, SteelSeries Aerox 5 editions, ASUS ROG Strix Scope RX TKL) and Logitech Centurion transport references.
- MagicKeyBattery (MIT License, https://github.com/fixtan/MagicKeyBattery) — Apple Magic Keyboard HID `GET_INPUT_REPORT` (`0x90`) battery protocol.
- rivalcfg (WTFPL v2, https://github.com/flozz/rivalcfg) and steel-mouse (MIT License, https://github.com/yurtemre7/steel-mouse) — SteelSeries Aerox 9 Wireless WoW Edition and Prime Mini Wireless USB product IDs.
- mouse-battery-tray (MIT License, https://github.com/incconutwo/mouse-battery-tray) — WLMouse Beast X (`0xA887`) product ID and Attack Shark X6 (`0xFA62` / model `0x85`) scaling and dock charging flag.
- ampere (GPL-2.0-or-later, https://github.com/crian/ampere) — CompX / DriverCore full-charge state (`0x02`), Dareu A950 PIDs, and MCHOSE RealTek frame length notes.
- Linux kernel HID subsystem (`drivers/hid/`, GPL-2.0, https://github.com/torvalds/linux) — protocol specifications and USB product IDs from `hid-nvidia-shield.c`, `hid-asus.c`, `hid-magicmouse.c`, `hid-apple.c`, `hid-logitech-hidpp.c`, `hid-playstation.c`, `hid-nintendo.c`, `hid-steam.c`, `hid-corsair-void.c`, and `hid-pulsar.c`.
- Community protocol documentation and references including GitHub user yiwluoq (ATK protocols), mitsimi/mchose-tray, Rapou7/offline-mchose (MCHOSE K7 documentation), and Fan4Metal/mouse_tray (Ninjutso Sora V2, ATK Zero Nordic 54L15 sleeping frame, Dareu A950, and Logitech `0x1004` slow-recharge protocol notes).
